c QIF benchmark 6/7: anonymous tally — 3-voter majority observable.
c
c Vars: 1=v1, 2=v2, 3=v3 (per-voter binary votes), 4=l (majority).
c Logic: l = majority(v1, v2, v3) = 1 iff at least 2 votes are YES.
c Observable l reveals tally>=2 but not which voters voted YES,
c preserving voter anonymity within each tally bucket.
c Models: 8 (one l value forced per (v1,v2,v3)).
c Channel: maps 8 vote profiles to 2 tally classes — leak of 1 bit
c of total tally information; 2 bits of voter identity remain hidden.
c
c Reference: Chaum D., "The Dining Cryptographers Problem" (J. Crypt.
c 1988) and follow-on anonymity-vote QIF analyses by Backes & Köpf.
p cnf 4 6
-1 -2 4 0
-1 -3 4 0
-2 -3 4 0
-4 1 2 0
-4 1 3 0
-4 2 3 0
